From 4ac6c1a8435dd2d08421d00177bb79a153b9a875 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:05:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 049/122] DXF: unknown objects and proxies as
 ACAD_PROXY_ENTITY/OBJECT, as AutoCAD

dwg2dxf skipped unknown entities and objects (AEC_*, TCH_*, ...), so the
DXF way (dwg2dxf, dxf2dwg) lost them. Write them, and the PROXY_* objects,
in AutoCAD's layout (the AC1027 gh109_1.dxf, the DXF reference):
90 498/499, 91 the class number in the order of the DXF CLASSES, the
drawing format 95 (R2018+: 71, 97), 70, the graphics 92/160 + 310 in
AcDbProxyEntity (no longer in AcDbEntity), the data: from R2007 on the
string stream 162 + 311 and the data before it 161 + 310, else 93 + 310,
the object ids 330 soft pointer, 340 hard pointer, 350 soft owner,
360 hard owner, and 94 0. in_dxf reads this back (add_PROXY) and joins
the data to the DWG layout, so dxf2dwg writes the same proxies as the
DWG way.

For gh109_1.dwg our DXF matches the CAD-written gh109_1.dxf in all 26
proxies (class name, drawing format, 70, the data and string bits, the
object ids); the graphics differ in 8, ours are those of the DWG.
gh109_1.dxf through dxf2dwg gives the same 26 proxies as the DWG way.

Also:
- the drawing format is version | maint << 16 (ODA spec, ACadSharp),
  was >> 8, also the R2018 version/maint pair;
- decode relative proxy object ids (6, 8, 10, 12) to absolute handles;
- the proxy extraction from unknown objects is shared
  (dwg_proxy_from_unknown), also for R2000 sources.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
